	"notes": "This is a design agency's homepage, and it is built as a stack of full-width bands rather than a grid: a big two-half hero (words on the left, a photo on the right, split exactly down the middle), then a scrolling list of services, a call-to-action strip, and a testimonial carousel that shows one quote at a time. The only place the page truly divides into side-by-side columns is that hero band, and even there the split is a clean 50/50 at every desktop width — it is not a fixed sidebar, it is two equal halves that both grow together. On a phone the hero simply stacks: the words on top, the photo underneath. The brief's scout guessed this page would turn out to be a `3-cards` layout, but nothing on it — at any of the four widths captured — ever arranges into a grid of cards; it stays a stack of single-column bands the whole way down.",
